Hello Locker routing team,

Thank you for your update on DL-016 and for offering the staffed Sedgeglass Counter or a locker retry after two days.

The recipient has told us she needs the parcel before the locker retry. We have sent her the Sedgeglass Counter option and asked her to confirm, and will tell you her choice as soon as we have it. To help her decide, could you please tell us:
1. Sedgeglass Counter's opening hours and the location details you normally give recipients;
2. How soon DL-016 could be ready for collection at the counter if she chooses it;
3. How long the counter would hold the parcel, and what the recipient needs to bring to collect it;
4. The exact date of the locker retry, if she does not choose the counter.

Kind regards,
Iona Quill
Rivet Delivery Desk

Hello,

Thank you for verified booking record DL-042. The consignee, Fenwick Spur, has no forklift, and its staff are not authorised to unload the pallet by hand. Please pass this to your carrier planner for a tail-lift option.

Conditions as stated in your booking record DL-042:
- one pallet, 280 kg;
- consignee has no forklift;
- consignee declares a level, hard-surfaced delivery bay and clear vehicle access.

Please confirm:
1. whether a tail-lift service is available for DL-042 under these conditions, and any further pallet or site details or conditions you need (I will get any extra details from the consignee);
2. the total extra cost to the consignee in GBP, including every surcharge and any tax, itemised;
3. the delivery date and time window that would apply.

This is a request for your option only; nothing is booked or accepted yet. The consignee's registered coordinator has given the desk authority to accept within a set budget, so once I have your full total I can confirm quickly.

Iona Quill
Rivet Delivery Desk

Hello,

Thank you for charge notice IC-047 for DL-047 (total GBP 32.00). The recipient, Teren Osk, has asked for an explanation before deciding what to do, specifically which part of the GBP 32.00 is handling and which part is the import assessment.

The itemisation is held by your billing team, so please pass this request to them and send me:
1. the itemised lines of IC-047, each with its description and amount in GBP;
2. a short plain-language explanation of what each line covers;
3. whether any payment or storage deadline applies to DL-047, and what happens to the shipment in the meantime;
4. how the recipient can query a line if they wish to.

I will pass your explanation to the recipient as you give it. The desk is not waiving, changing or interpreting any line of the charge.

Iona Quill
Rivet Delivery Desk
